# PROVENANCE: measured, not generated. Every response byte below was captured
# from a genuine DESFire EV1 8K over PC/SC by a PC/SC capture tool
# and is used here as an expectation for our emulator. As with the other
# hardware_genuine_*.vec files, this vector is the opposite of the rest
# of the corpus: the others were recorded from the reference engine, so they
# pin what we decided; this one pins what the silicon does. A mismatch here is
# either a real divergence or a difference we can justify in writing, never a
# vector to be re-recorded from our engine.
#
# Card: UID 04304622216A80, hardware 1.0, software 1.4, storage 8K. Formatted
# with FormatPICC under the all-zero PICC test key, then provisioned with
# a synthetic structure whose every key is a published test key. That is what
# makes an authenticated capture safe to commit and replayable: no key material
# enters the tree, and our engine derives the same session key from the same
# pinned nonces.
#
# RndA is the fixed constant the recorder uses; RndB is the card's, recovered
# by decrypting its first authentication frame with the test key and
# pinned here with inject-random so our engine offers the same challenge.
# What this vector is for: record files in every communication mode.
#   file 01 (linear plain): record 5 refused with BE
#   file 01 (linear plain): 4 records read back, oldest to newest [0, 1, 2, 3]
#   file 11 (cyclic plain): 3 records read back, oldest to newest [2, 3, 4]
#   file 02 (linear MACed): record 5 refused with BE
#   file 02 (linear MACed): 4 records read back, oldest to newest [0, 1, 2, 3]
#   file 12 (cyclic MACed): 3 records read back, oldest to newest [2, 3, 4]
#   file 03 (linear enciphered): record 5 refused with BE
#   file 03 (linear enciphered): 4 records read back, oldest to newest [0, 1, 2, 3]
#   file 13 (cyclic enciphered): 3 records read back, oldest to newest [2, 3, 4]
#   a cleared record file answers ReadRecords with BE

name: genuine EV1 8K, linear and cyclic record files under a D40 session
origin: physical-card
uid: 04304622216A80
picc-key-settings-1: 0F
picc-key-settings-2: 01
picc-auth-mode: D40
picc-key-len: 16
requires: ev1,record-files
picc-generation: EV1
picc-storage: 8192

scan
# An application with two keys; key 1 owns every record file below.
status   90CA000005F3F2F10F0200 => 00
status   905A000003F3F2F100 => 00
#
# A linear and a cyclic record file per communication mode, with
# 16-octet records and room for four.
status   90C100000A0100111110000004000000 => 00
status   90C000000A1100111110000004000000 => 00
status   90C100000A0201111110000004000000 => 00
status   90C000000A1201111110000004000000 => 00
status   90C100000A0303111110000004000000 => 00
status   90C000000A1303111110000004000000 => 00
#
# Authenticate as key 1.
inject-random 8E9128D1DB5FE195
exchange native-apdu 900A0000010100 => 7BF5165DB98C58F891AF
exchange native-apdu 90AF00001005EEC31F1E6A0CC3D6D7FCF1B92A194300 => 26ACED3C771EF9A09100
#
# File 01, linear, plain: five records written and committed one at a time,
# one more than the file holds, then every record read at once.
exchange native-apdu 903B000017010000001000001010101010101010101010101010101000 => 9100
exchange native-apdu 90C7000000 => 9100
exchange native-apdu 903B000017010000001000001111111111111111111111111111111100 => 9100
